  "executive_summary": "Bańbura, Giannone, and Reichlin show that a VAR can include many macro variables if shrinkage increases with system size. The prior is scaled relative to a small-model fit and may include sum-of-coefficients and dummy-initial-observation components. Forecast comparisons and a monetary-policy exercise demonstrate the value of a large information set, but hyperparameters must be chosen inside training data and stability and residual diagnostics remain mandatory.",
